steps.explanation:
The data must leave the first flip-flop, cross the logic and be set up before the next edge:
$T_{min} = t_{cq} + t_{pd} + t_{su}$ = {{tcq|s}} + {{tpd|s}} + {{tsu|s}} = {{tcq+tpd+tsu|s}}
$f_{max} = 1/T_{min}$ = **{{1/(tcq+tpd+tsu)|Hz}}**.

The slowest path ends at $T_{ {{n-1}} }$, which passes through $n - 2$ = {{n-2}} AND gates.
$T_{min} = t_{cq} + (n-2)\,t_{AND} + t_{su}$ = {{tcq|s}} + {{n-2}} × {{tand|s}} + {{tsu|s}} = {{tcq+(n-2)*tand+tsu|s}}
$f_{max}$ = **{{1/(tcq+(n-2)*tand+tsu)|Hz}}**. Computing all $T_i$ with wide AND gates in parallel would make $f_{max}$ almost independent of $n$.
